      'Rule example: In Partner: your team aims to win 6 points while the opponents have 0 (six love). In Cut Throat: be first to 6 wins provided another player has 0. Win a hand by playing all your bones or by having fewest spots when the game is blocked.',
      'Turn-flow example: Play is anti-clockwise. Each turn a player plays one bone to extend one of the two ends of the layout; touching ends must match. Doubles are played at right angles. If a player cannot play they pass (no draw in standard block style for Partner; Cut Throat follows same play). The hand ends when one player empties their hand or the game blocks. Winning team scores 1 point; playing the key bone (only playable bone when both ends are hard) scores 2.',
